# era-bank — UI rules

Applies to `era-bank/app/**` and `era-bank/src/components/**`.

## Modal CRUD (mandatory)

Follow [docs/UI_PLAYBOOK_SATELLITES.md](../../docs/UI_PLAYBOOK_SATELLITES.md):

- **One index route per entity area** — list/table on the page.
- **Create, detail, edit, and workflow actions** open in `OpsModalShell` (wraps `@era/satellite-kit/ui` `ModalShell`).
- **Do not add** standalone `/new` or `/[id]` pages for admin/ops entities. Use redirects with `?modal=create` / `?id=` for bookmarks only.
- Row click → detail modal; primary «Add» → create modal.

Shared primitives: `era-bank/src/components/ops/` — `useOpsModal`, `OpsDataTable`, `OpsModalShell`, `EodLockProvider`.

## EOD lock

- All mutation submit buttons must respect `useEodLock().mutationsDisabled` (wired in `OpsModalShell` and explicit actions).
- `EodLockProvider` wraps ops shell; polls `GET /api/eod/{today}`.

## Entitlements

- Sidebar nav filtered via `useBankEntitlements()` — hide modules when `banking_*` not active.
- BFF routes enforce entitlement server-side; UI filter is UX only.

## i18n

- Locales: az (default), ru, en — keys in `messages/*.json`; no raw enum labels in UI.
- New screens: add keys to **all three** locale files in the same change.

## BFF

- No ledger/money persistence in `era_bank` DB (ADR D9).
- GL reads/writes via `/api/gl/*`, not `/api/accounts/gl/*`.

## Module map

Ops screens by route — see app `PRD.md` §modules and [docs/BANK_DOC_API_UI_AUDIT.md](../../docs/BANK_DOC_API_UI_AUDIT.md).
